    {
      "number": 42,
      "source_text_sha256": "641ca1f5ec3d7d3be78ba5a6ab675f7d92cd9197513dd23fecc04c1622784cde",
      "lines": [
        "Recall: How Neural Networks Learn",
        "• Repeat until stopping criterion met:",
        "1. Forward pass: propagate",
        "training data through model",
        "to make prediction",
        "2. Quantify the dissatisfaction",
        "with a model’s results on the",
        "training data",
        "3. Backward pass: using",
        "predicted output, calculate",
        "gradients backward to assign",
        "blame to each model",
        "parameter",
        "4. Update each parameter",
        "using calculated gradients",
        "Figure from: Atilim Gunes Baydin, Barak A. Pearlmutter, Alexey Andreyevich Radul,",
        "Jeffrey Mark Siskind; Automatic Differentiation in Machine Learning: a Survey; 2018"
      ]
    },
